---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Each moment is told from the visitor's side. The closing line lowers the temperature; it never argues back.
const moments = [
  {
    moment: "You read the wall label three times and still don't know what it means.",
    felt: 'Like everyone else took a class you missed.',
    actually: "Art has its own dialect, and some people use it to sound important rather than to explain. If a sentence about a painting could just as easily describe a toaster, it isn't saying much.",
    notYou: "Clear writing about art exists. That label just isn't it.",
    say: "\u201cI'll be honest, the label lost me. What do you notice first when you look at it?\u201d",
  },
  {
    moment: 'You asked a simple question and got a sigh.',
    felt: "Like you'd gotten something wrong.",
    actually: "To the artist, your question meant they'd have to explain themselves. Behind the sigh is one of two thoughts: \u201cThis person doesn't get it,\u201d or \u201cDid I make this too complicated for everybody?\u201d Either way, it's about them, not you.",
    notYou: 'Being willing to ask is the part that takes nerve.',
    say: "\u201cNo rush. I'm just curious where you started.\u201d Or just keep looking. The work might answer for them.",
  },
  {
    moment: 'They told you that you \u201cjust don\u2019t get it.\u201d',
    felt: 'A door closing.',
    actually: "It's a way to end a conversation before it gets uncomfortable for them, often because they've been misunderstood before and expect it again.",
    notYou: 'Nobody gets a piece on the first try. Sometimes not even the person who made it.',
    say: "\u201cThat's fair. I'm going to look a little longer.\u201d Then do. No reply needed.",
  },
  {
    moment: "At their own opening, the artist wouldn't meet your eye.",
    felt: "Snobbery. Like you weren't worth their time.",
    actually: 'Openings are terrifying: a room full of people deciding whether your work is any good. Aloof is often just armor.',
    notYou: "They're probably hoping someone will say something kind.",
    say: '\u201cThanks for putting this up. I liked the one by the door.\u201d Specific and small beats clever.',
  },
  {
    moment: 'Everyone nodded along to the artist talk, so you nodded too.',
    felt: 'Like you were the only one faking it.',
    actually: "You probably weren't. A lot of talk about art is a performance, and the audience performs right back. Half the room is nodding for the same reason you are.",
    notYou: 'If you had raised your hand, three people would have been grateful.',
    say: '\u201cCould you say a little more about how you actually made it?\u201d Questions about process are safe ground for everyone.',
  },
  {
    moment: 'You mentioned a painting you love, and someone smirked.',
    felt: 'Like your taste was cheap.',
    actually: "Some art people treat pretty or comfortable art as lesser, usually because they worry about being seen as lesser themselves. It's a status game, not a judgment about you.",
    notYou: 'Loving art you can live with is the whole point of having art at home.',
    say: "\u201cI like having it around. What do you keep on your walls?\u201d",
  },
  {
    moment: "You were told it's supposed to be difficult.",
    felt: 'Like difficulty was the test, and you failed it.',
    actually: "Some good art is hard. But \u201cit's supposed to be hard\u201d can also be a way of skipping the question of whether it's any good, or whether it's meant to make you feel anything.",
    notYou: "Difficult and meaningful aren't the same thing. You're allowed to want both.",
    say: "\u201cIs there a way in you'd suggest for someone seeing it cold?\u201d",
  },
  {
    moment: 'You said something mild, and the artist bristled.',
    felt: "Like you'd insulted them without meaning to.",
    actually: 'For a lot of artists, the work and the self are the same thing. A comment about the painting lands as a comment about them.',
    notYou: "You touched a sore spot you couldn't have seen.",
    say: "\u201cI didn't mean that as a knock. There's a lot here I'm still taking in.\u201d Or let it go and move on. That's allowed.",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="What's a Jerk? - Artists Are Jerks" bodyClass="whats-a-jerk-page">
  <div class="jerk-page">
    <header class="jerk-header">
      <h1>What's a Jerk?</h1>
      <p class="lede">You know the type, or you've heard about them: the moody artist in black who looks at you like you've just asked where the bathroom is. So, are artists jerks? Some are. Some are the good kind. And some aren't jerks at all.</p>
    </header>

    <ul class="kinds">
      <li class="kind kind--good"><h2>Good jerks</h2><p>They make you see something you'd have walked right past. They're annoying on purpose, and it's usually worth it.</p><p class="kind-example">The painter whose work bugs you for a week.</p></li>
      <li class="kind kind--bad"><h2>Bad jerks</h2><p>They make you feel dumb so they can feel important. That's the stereotype, and yes, they're real.</p><p class="kind-example">"You wouldn't understand."</p></li>
      <li class="kind kind--normie"><h2>Normies</h2><p>Not jerks at all. They make art you can live with, and they keep it in everyday life. Art needs them more than it admits.</p><p class="kind-example">The landscape over your parents' couch.</p></li>
    </ul>

    <section class="bad-section" aria-labelledby="bad-title">
      <h2 id="bad-title" class="section-title">When an artist is being a bad jerk</h2>
      <p class="section-intro">Eight moments people run into around art, what was really going on, and a gentle way to keep talking if you want to.</p>
    <ol class="behaviors">
      {moments.map((item, index) => (
        <li class="card">
          <h3 class="card-title"><span class="card-number" aria-hidden="true">{index + 1}</span>{item.moment}</h3>
          <h4 class="card-label">What it felt like</h4>
          <p>{item.felt}</p>
          <h4 class="card-label">What was actually going on</h4>
          <p>{item.actually}</p>
          <p class="not-you"><strong>It's not you.</strong> {item.notYou}</p>
          <div class="keep-talking">
            <h4 class="card-label">If you want to keep talking</h4>
            <p class="card-quote">{item.say}</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>

    </section>

    <aside class="artist-note">
      <h2>If you're an artist</h2>
      <p>And you recognized yourself in a few of these: welcome. So did we. <a href="/thinking-like-an-artist/">Thinking Like an Artist →</a></p>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <style>
    .jerk-page { max-width: var(--max-width-text); margin: 0 auto; padding: var(--space-4) 0 var(--space-12); }
    .jerk-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
    .jerk-header h1 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--font-size-4xl); color: var(--color-black); }
    .lede { max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto; text-align: left; font-size: var(--font-size-lg); line-height: var(--line-height-normal); color: var(--color-black); }
    .behaviors { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .card { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5); background: var(--color-cream); border: var(--border-base) solid var(--color-black); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); color: var(--color-black); }
    .card p { margin: 0; font-size: var(--font-size-base); line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed); }
    .card p + p { margin-top: var(--space-3); }
    .card-title { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-3); margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--font-size-xl); line-height: var(--line-height-tight); }
    .card-number { display: grid; place-items: center; flex: none; width: var(--space-8); height: var(--space-8); border-radius: var(--radius-full); background: var(--color-black); color: var(--color-gold); font-size: var(--font-size-base); }
    .card-label { margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-1); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); color: var(--color-purple); }
    .card-quote { font-style: normal; }
    .card .not-you { margin-top: var(--space-3); padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3); background: var(--color-green); border-radius: var(--radius-base); }
    .keep-talking { margin-top: var(--space-3); padding-top: var(--space-1); border-top: var(--border-thin) solid var(--color-black); }
    .kinds { display: grid; gap: var(--space-3); margin: 0 0 var(--space-8); padding: 0; list-style: none; }
    .kind { padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5); border: var(--border-base) solid var(--color-black); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); color: var(--color-black); }
    .kind h2 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-1); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); }
    .kind p { margin: 0; line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed); }
    .kind .kind-example { margin-top: var(--space-2); font-style: italic; }
    .kind--good { background: var(--color-green); }
    .kind--bad { background: var(--color-plum-red); color: var(--color-white); }
    .kind--normie { background: var(--color-cream); }
    .section-title { margin: 0 0 var(--space-1); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--font-size-2xl); }
    .section-intro { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed); }
    .artist-note { margin-top: var(--space-6); padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5); background: var(--color-black); border-radius: var(--radius-lg); color: var(--color-white); }
    .artist-note h2 { margin: 0 0 var(--space-1); font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: var(--font-size-xl); color: var(--color-gold); }
    .artist-note p { margin: 0; line-height: var(--line-height-relaxed); }
    .artist-note a { color: var(--color-gold); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); }
    @media (min-width: 900px) {
      .jerk-page { max-width: var(--max-width-content); }
      .jerk-header h1 { font-size: var(--font-size-5xl); }
      .behaviors { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      .kinds { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
